# __libc_csu_init and __libc_csu_fini Functions

Based on the glibc source file, here are the two function implementations:

## __libc_csu_init

```c
void
__libc_csu_init (int argc, char **argv, char **envp)
{
 /* For dynamically linked executables the preinit array is executed by
 the dynamic linker (before initializing any shared object). */

#ifndef LIBC_NONSHARED
 /* For static executables, preinit happens right before init. */
 {
 const size_t size = __preinit_array_end - __preinit_array_start;
 size_t i;
 for (i = 0; i < size; i++)
 (*__preinit_array_start [i]) (argc, argv, envp);
 }
#endif

#ifndef NO_INITFINI
 _init ();
#endif

 const size_t size = __init_array_end - __init_array_start;
 for (size_t i = 0; i < size; i++)
 (*__init_array_start [i]) (argc, argv, envp);
}
```

## __libc_csu_fini

```c
void
__libc_csu_fini (void)
{
#ifndef LIBC_NONSHARED
 size_t i = __fini_array_end - __fini_array_start;
 while (i-- > 0)
 (*__fini_array_start [i]) ();

# ifndef NO_INITFINI
 _fini ();
# endif
#endif
}
```

These functions handle initializer and finalizer array execution during program startup and shutdown respectively.

